1. Create an instance of the AEAD GCM cipher class with the desired key and nonce.
2. Call the `updateAAD` method with the additional data (Associated Data) that you want to include in the authentication process.
3. Use the updated cipher object to encrypt or decrypt data as needed.

Here's some sample code demonstrating how to use the `updateAAD` method:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <cryptopp/aeadgcm.h>

int main() {
    std::string key = "my_secret_key";
    std::string nonce = "my_nonce";
    std::string additional_data = "this is my additional data";

    CryptoPP::AES::GCM gcm(CryptoPP::AES::GCM::DEFAULT_KEY_LENGTH);
    gcm.SetKey(key);
    gcm.SetNonce(nonce);

    gcm.UpdateAAD(additional_data);

    // Encrypt some data
    std::string plaintext = "This is some sensitive data.";
    std::vector<unsigned char> ciphertext = gcm.Encrypt(plaintext);

    // Decrypt the data
    std::vector<unsigned char> decrypted_data = gcm.Decrypt(ciphertext);
    std::string decrypted_plaintext = std::string(decrypted_data.begin(), decrypted_data.end());

    std::cout << "Decrypted plaintext: " << decrypted_plaintext << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```
