To deploy a React Native app to TestFlight, follow these steps:

1. Set up your development environment:
   - Install Node.js and npm (Node Package Manager) from https://nodejs.org/
   - Install Xcode from the Mac App Store for iOS development
   - Install Android Studio and the Android SDK (Software Development Kit) for Android development

2. Create a new React Native project:
   - Run `npx react-native init MyApp` (replace "MyApp" with your desired project name)
   - Navigate to the project directory with `cd MyApp`

3. Set up the project for iOS and Android:
   - In `MyApp/ios`, create a new file named `AppDelegate.m` and add the following code:
     ```objective-c
     #import "ReactNative/RCTBridgeModule.h"
     #import "ReactNative/RCTRootView.h"

     @implementation AppDelegate

     - (BOOL)application:(UIApplication *)app didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:(NSDictionary *)launchOptions {
       RCTRootView *rootView = [[RCTRootView alloc] initWithBundleURL:[NSBundle mainBundle]];
       rootView.bridge = [[RCTBridge alloc] initWithDelegate:self launchOptions:launchOptions];
       self.window = [[UIWindow alloc] initWithFrame:[UIScreen mainScreen].bounds];
       self.window.rootViewController = rootView;
       [self.window makeKeyAndVisible];
       return YES;
     }

     @end
     ```
   - In `MyApp/android`, create a new file named `MainActivity.java` and add the following code:
     ```java
     import com.facebook.react.ReactActivity;

     public class MainActivity extends ReactActivity {
       @Override
       protected void onCreate(Bundle savedInstanceState) {
         super.onCreate(savedInstanceState);
         setContentView(R.layout.activity_main);
       }
     }
     ```

4. Install required dependencies:
   - For iOS, run `npm install --save react-native-vector-icons` to install the vector icons library

