To generate recurring events, you can use a library like `java-time` to parse and manipulate dates. Here's an example code snippet using `java-time`:

```java
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;

public class RecurringEvents {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        LocalDate startDate = LocalDate.of(2022, 1, 1);
        LocalDate endDate = LocalDate.of(2022, 1, 10);
        int interval = 1; // Daily

        for (LocalDate date = startDate; date.isBefore(endDate); date = date.plusDays(interval)) {
            System.out.println("Event on " + date);
        }
    }
}
