```

4. Use JavaScript to add a tooltip to the `div` element when hovered over:

```javascript
const professionalText = document.querySelector('.professional-text');

professionalText.addEventListener('mouseover', () => {
  const tooltip = document.createElement('div');
  tooltip.classList.add('tooltip');
  tooltip.innerHTML = 'Congratulations on your outstanding achievement!';
  professionalText.appendChild(tooltip);
});

professionalText.addEventListener('mouseout', () => {
  const tooltip = document.querySelector('.tooltip');
  if (tooltip) {
    professionalText.removeChild(tooltip);
  }
});
```

This solution will enhance the message's impact by making it stand out and providing additional information when hovered over. The layout and other content will be preserved, as the changes are made only to the `div` element and its styles.

