Here's a simple HTML page with a button to display the background image of the user's computer on the desktop:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Display Background Image</title>
    <style>
        body {
            text-align: center;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px 20px;
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Display Background Image</h1>
    <button onclick="displayBackgroundImage()">Display Background Image</button>
    <script>
        function displayBackgroundImage() {
            const backgroundImage = document.createElement('img');
            backgroundImage.src = chrome.runtime.getURL('background.jpg');
            backgroundImage.style.position = 'absolute';
            backgroundImage.style.top = '0';
            backgroundImage.style.left = '0';
            backgroundImage.style.width = '100%';
            backgroundImage.style.height = '100%';
            document.body.appendChild(backgroundImage);
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a button that, when clicked, will display the background image of the user's computer on the desktop. The background image is loaded from a file named "background.jpg" in the Chrome extension directory. You can replace this file with your own background image.

Note that this code requires you to have a Chrome extension installed and configured. You can create a new Chrome extension by following the instructions in the Chrome Developer Documentation: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/mv3/getstarted/

