The given MATLAB code calculates the distance between two points on the Earth's surface, taking into account the Earth's elliptical shape. Here's the code with comments explaining each step:

```matlab
% Earth's semi-major axis in meters
a = 6378137;

% Earth's semi-minor axis in meters
b = 6356752.3142;

% Latitude of point 1 in degrees
lat1 = deg2rad(37.7749);

% Longitude of point 1 in degrees
lon1 = deg2rad(-122.4194);

% Latitude of point 2 in degrees
lat2 = deg2rad(51.5074);

% Longitude of point 2 in degrees
lon2 = deg2rad(-0.1278);

% Earth's flattening
f = (a-b)/a;

% Earth's eccentricity squared
e2 = 2*f - f^2;

% Radius of curvature in the prime vertical at point 1
N1 = a/sqrt(1-e2*sin(lat1)^2);

% Radius of curvature in the prime vertical at point 2
N2 = a/sqrt(1-e2*sin(lat2)^2);

