To prevent the planets from being too close together, you can implement a simple check before adding a new planet to the array. You can use the `checkCollision` function from the Three.js library to detect collisions between the new planet and all existing planets. If a collision is detected, you can simply generate a new set of random coordinates until a non-colliding position is found.

Here's an updated version of your `generateRandomPlanets` function that includes this check:
```javascript
const generateRandomPlanets = (numPlanets, minDistance) => {
  const planets = [];
  let attempts = 0;

  while (planets.length < numPlanets && attempts < 100) {
    attempts++;

    const planet = {
      position: [
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
